  "limits": [
    "Native accepted ECH + PSK + early GET are now verified together on one connection, including independent client/server Finished checks and HTTP/3 200.",
    "The matched Surf/native Google early HEADERS bytes and dynamic encoder instructions agree exactly. HTTP/3 selection is forced only for the isolated Surf replay, with Alt-Used disabled to reproduce the captured fields.",
    "Early stream interleaving and QPACK instruction packet grouping still differ in this sample; no identical packet schedule is claimed. Native opaque fetch also sends STOP_SENDING, whereas Surf consumes the response body.",
    "Normal navigation and same-origin fetch can produce control-only 0-RTT or a legitimate HTTP/2 winner; an early GET is not guaranteed on every request.",
    "Native real-browser NIC captures are inside Linux Docker; they do not establish Windows OS packet behavior or matching physical-host NIC pacing.",
    "Raw pcaps, NSS secrets, live tickets and browser profiles remain private."
  ],
